From 3723adc19dfe208ab31b65abf37933964aeaeba8 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Giuseppe Maggio <jertlok@proton.me>
Date: Tue, 15 Sep 2026 10:10:30 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 03/10] pmb.parse.apkbuild: evaluate $CARCH conditionals for
 the target arch

abuild sources an APKBUILD with CARCH set, and many aports choose
dependencies and subpackages that way. Alpine's mesa, for example, adds
clang-dev, libclc-dev, rust, rust-bindgen and spirv-llvm-translator-dev to
makedepends and mesa-rusticl to subpackages inside
'case "$CARCH" in armv7|aarch64|x86|x86_64|loongarch64)'. pmbootstrap's
parser does not run shell code, so it never saw them: the build chroot
lacked bindgen and mesa failed with "Program 'bindgen' not found".

Add an optional arch to pmb.parse.apkbuild(), and when it is given,
rewrite the lines first (pmb/parse/_apkbuild_cond.py): every top-level
case, if/elif/else and "[ ... ] && ... || ..." list whose conditions can be
decided exactly is replaced by the commands of the branch the shell would
take. Conditions may use $CARCH, $CTARGET_ARCH and variables assigned
earlier in the APKBUILD; tests support =, ==, !=, -n, -z, the integer
comparisons and !. Subpackage functions get the same treatment, where all
branches used to apply at once. Anything that cannot be decided without
running the shell (command substitutions, loops, $CBUILD or $BOOTSTRAP,
here-documents) leaves that block exactly as it was, and a file that cannot
be tokenized is not changed at all.

Pass the arch where it is known: pmaports.get(), package.get() (used by
depends_recurse() for installs) and the build queue, which now re-parses
the APKBUILD once the build arch is decided. Callers without an arch get
the previous result.

An int attribute that is not a number, like openjdk's
provider_priority=$((_majorver + 1)) inside such a block, now parses as 0
instead of raising.

Checked against busybox sh sourcing all 14418 APKBUILDs of Alpine's
aports and pmaports for nine architectures: 3237 attributes in 607 aports
that were wrong are now right, none that were right changed, and no parse
raises that did not before.

Assisted-by: Claude
